{
    "map": {
        "collection_builder.descr": "<xdoc><p>The input image collection. It can be seen as a template that contains arguments such as the source mosaic dataset path, filters to extract a subset from the input data source, and so on.</p><p>Currently, this tool only supports <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Simple Collection</span>, which allows you to define a single data source and a query filter, for the data source.</p><ul><li><span title=\"SIMPLE_COLLECTION\">Simple collection</span>—Allows you to define a data source and a query filter.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "collection_builder.domain.SIMPLE_COLLECTION": "Simple collection",
        "collection_builder.title": "Collection Builder",
        "collection_builder_arguments.descr": "<xdoc><p>The list of arguments to create a subset collection of the mosaic dataset.</p><p>This tool only supports the data source and filter to subset the mosaic dataset. The <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Data Source</span> and <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Where Clause</span> values must be completed, otherwise the tool cannot be executed.</p><ul><li><span title=\"DataSource\">Data Source</span>—The path of the data source.</li><li><span title=\"WhereClause\">Where Clause</span>—The filter used to subset the mosaic dataset.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "collection_builder_arguments.dt.title1": "Name",
        "collection_builder_arguments.dt.title2": "Value",
        "collection_builder_arguments.title": "Collection Builder Arguments",
        "collection_properties.descr": "<xdoc><p>The output mosaic dataset key properties.</p><p>The key metadata properties that are available is based on the type of sensor that captured the imagery. Some examples of key metadata properties include the following:<ul><li>SensorName</li><li>ProductName</li><li>AcquisitionDate</li><li>CloudCover</li><li>SunAzimuth</li><li>SunElevation</li><li>SensorAzimuth</li><li>SensorElevation</li><li>Off-nadirAngle</li><li>BandName</li><li>MinimumWavelength</li><li>MaximumWavelength</li><li>RadianceGain</li><li>RadianceBias</li><li>SolarIrradiance</li><li>ReflectanceGain</li><li>ReflectanceBias</li></ul></p></xdoc>",
        "collection_properties.dt.title1": "Name",
        "collection_properties.dt.title2": "Value",
        "collection_properties.title": "Raster Collection Properties",
        "description": "Performs batch analysis or processing on image collections contained in a mosaic dataset. The images in the input mosaic dataset can be processed individually or as groups.",
        "format.descr": "<xdoc><p>The format type of the raster to be generated.</p><ul><li><span title=\"TIFF\">Tiff</span>—Tagged Image File Format (TIFF)</li><li><span title=\"IMAGINE Image\">ERDAS IMAGINE</span>—ERDAS IMAGINE file</li><li><span title=\"CRF\">CRF</span>—Cloud Raster Format. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"MRF\">MRF</span>—Meta Raster Format</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "format.domain.CRF": "CRF",
        "format.domain.IMAGINE Image": "ERDAS IMAGINE",
        "format.domain.MRF": "MRF",
        "format.domain.TIFF": "Tiff",
        "format.title": "Format",
        "generate_rasters.descr": "<xdoc><p>Generate raster dataset files of the mosaic dataset items, after the application of the RFT.<ul><li>Unchecked—The processing defined by the raster function template will be appended to the image items from the input data source to produce an image item in the output mosaic dataset. This is the default.</li><li>Checked—Create raster datasets on disk. You will also need to specify the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Output Raster Workspace</span> and <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Format</span>.</li></ul></p></xdoc>",
        "generate_rasters.title": "Generate Rasters",
        "out_base_name.descr": "<xdoc><p>Defines the output base name of the persisted raster datasets, if the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Generate Rasters</span> parameter is checked on. Multiple raster dataset outputs will have a number alias appended to their base name.</p><p>The resulting mosaic dataset will reference the CRF directly without maintaining the raster function chain.</p></xdoc>",
        "out_base_name.title": "Output Base Name",
        "out_raster_collection.descr": "The full path of the mosaic dataset to be created. The mosaic dataset must be stored in a geodatabase.",
        "out_raster_collection.title": "Output Raster Collection",
        "out_workspace.descr": "<xdoc><p>Defines the output location for the persisted raster datasets, if the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Generate Rasters</span> parameter is checked on.</p><p>The naming convention for the output raster files is oid_&lt;oid#&gt;_&lt;Unique_GUID&gt;.</p></xdoc>",
        "out_workspace.title": "Output Raster Workspace",
        "params.category1": "Output Collection Options",
        "raster_function.descr": "<xdoc><p>The path to a raster function template file (.rft.xml or .rft.json). The raster function template will be applied to every item in the input mosaic dataset. The <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Function Editor</span> can be used to create the template. If no RFT is defined, this tool will create the output mosaic based on the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Collection Builder Arguments</span> parameter.</p></xdoc>",
        "raster_function.title": "Input Raster Function",
        "raster_function_arguments.descr": "<xdoc><p>The parameters associated with the function chain.</p><p>For example, if the function chain applies the NDVI function, set the visible and infrared IDs. The raster variable name of the RFT should be the <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">Tag</span> field value in the input data source.</p></xdoc>",
        "raster_function_arguments.dt.title1": "Name",
        "raster_function_arguments.dt.title2": "Value",
        "raster_function_arguments.title": "Raster Function Arguments",
        "summary": "<xdoc><p>Performs batch analysis or processing on image collections contained in a mosaic dataset. The images in the input mosaic dataset can be processed individually or as groups.</p><p>The rules of processing can be defined through the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Collection Builder</span> parameter and raster function parameters. It generates a new mosaic dataset of processed images. You can optionally choose to save the processed images to disk as separate files. The default condition is to append the input raster function to the mosaic dataset&apos;s existing images&apos; function chain, and add it to the output mosaic dataset.</p></xdoc>",
        "title": "Generate Raster Collection"
    }
}
